---
import ShowcaseLayout from '../layouts/ShowcaseLayout.astro';
import SpecimenPreview from '../components/SpecimenPreview.astro';
const brand = [['50','#faf5f2'],['200','#e9c6b9'],['400','#d97757'],['500','#c96442'],['600','#be5c3a'],['700','#b55333'],['800','#964225'],['950','#3f1b10']];
const roles = [
  ['Background','#f5f4ed','#141413'],['Foreground','#141413','#faf9f5'],['Card','#faf9f5','#30302e'],
  ['Secondary / muted / input','#e8e6dc','#30302e'],['Muted foreground','#5e5d59','#b0aea5'],
  ['Border','#f0eee6','#30302e'],['Ring','#d1cfc5','#b0aea5'],['Destructive','#b53333','#b53333'],
];
---
<ShowcaseLayout title="Foundations" description="Color, type, space, geometry and motion for Terracotta Minimalist Brutalism.">
  <section class="page-intro page-width"><p class="eyebrow">THE SHARED LANGUAGE</p><h1>Foundations.</h1><p>Warmth in the surfaces. Precision in the structure. A small set of decisions that carries through every component.</p></section>
  <nav class="section-index page-width" aria-label="Foundation index">{['Color','Typography','Space','Structure','Focus','Motion'].map(label => <a href={`#${label.toLowerCase()}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav>
  <div class="foundations-grid page-width">
    <section id="color" class="foundation-panel wide-specimen"><p class="eyebrow">01 / COLOR</p><h2>Terracotta, in good measure.</h2><p>A warm accent family for emphasis and feedback. Neutral surfaces do most of the work.</p><div class="swatch-grid">{brand.map(([step,color]) => <figure><div class="color-swatch" style={`background:${color}`} /><figcaption><strong>Brand {step}</strong><code>{color}</code></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
      <div class="surface-pair"><div data-theme="light"><p class="eyebrow">LIGHT</p><h3>Parchment & ivory.</h3><p>Near-black text on a warm reading surface.</p><span class="surface-example">A quiet card surface</span></div><div data-theme="dark"><p class="eyebrow">DARK</p><h3>Warm charcoal.</h3><p>Ivory text with the same sharp structure.</p><span class="surface-example">A quiet card surface</span></div></div>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-alternative"><caption>Semantic color roles · light and dark</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{roles.map(([role,light,dark]) => <tr><th scope="row">{role}</th><td><code>{light}</code></td><td><code>{dark}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="foundation-note">Subtle surface borders define grouping. Controls use a stronger boundary and focus outline so they stay easy to locate. Brand 400 and 500 are accents; small text uses darker terracotta in light mode.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="typography" class="foundation-panel wide-specimen"><p class="eyebrow">02 / TYPOGRAPHY</p><h2>Two voices. One rhythm.</h2><p>Lexend Deca gives headings a deliberate, geometric shape. Inclusive Sans keeps descriptions and controls open and readable.</p><div class="type-specimens"><div><span>DISPLAY / LEXEND DECA</span><p class="type-display">Less noise.<br />More intent.</p></div><div><span>HEADING / LEXEND DECA</span><p class="type-heading">Useful by design.</p></div><div><span>BODY / INCLUSIVE SANS</span><p class="type-body">Give the important things enough room. A clear label and a little context make the next action easier.</p></div><div><span>METADATA / SYSTEM MONOSPACE</span><code>01 / COLLECTIONS / PREVIEW</code></div></div><dl class="type-scale"><div><dt>Display</dt><dd>44–72px · 1.12 · 500</dd></div><div><dt>Section</dt><dd>28–40px · 1.25 · 500</dd></div><div><dt>Component</dt><dd>20–24px · 1.3 · 500</dd></div><div><dt>Body</dt><dd>16px · 1.6 · 400</dd></div></dl></section>
    <section id="space" class="foundation-panel"><p class="eyebrow">03 / SPACE</p><h2>Room to breathe.</h2><p>A four-pixel rhythm scales from small control gaps to generous section spacing.</p><div class="spacing-scale">{[4,8,12,16,24,32,48,64,96].map(size => <div><code>{size}px</code><span style={`width:${size}px`} /></div>)}</div></section>
    <section id="structure" class="foundation-panel"><p class="eyebrow">04 / STRUCTURE</p><h2>Sharp, by default.</h2><p>Zero-radius cards, fields, buttons and overlays. Circles serve a function in avatars, radio controls and status dots.</p><div class="structure-sample"><div><span>01</span><strong>1px borders.<br />A clear edge.</strong></div><div><span>02</span><strong>No ordinary<br />surface shadow.</strong></div></div><p class="foundation-note">The page container reaches 1280px. Bento layouts recompose into fewer columns as space narrows. Media keeps its frame and aspect ratio.</p></section>
    <section id="focus" class="foundation-panel"><p class="eyebrow">05 / FOCUS & STATES</p><h2>A clear way through.</h2><p>Tab to the controls below. A strong terracotta outline locates focus. Labels, explicit errors and status text carry meaning alongside color.</p><SpecimenPreview slug="button" /><SpecimenPreview slug="validation" /></section>
    <section id="motion" class="foundation-panel"><p class="eyebrow">06 / MOTION</p><h2>Movement with a reason.</h2><p>Interaction feedback takes 150–300ms. A reveal takes 400–700ms, with short travel and a calm ease. Content stays readable before hydration.</p><SpecimenPreview slug="reveal" /><a class="text-link" href="/motion/">Explore motion studies ↗</a></section>
  </div>
</ShowcaseLayout>
